  "generated_description": "<div class=\"mountain-description prose prose-stone max-w-none\">\n  <p>At 978 feet, <strong>Battle Point</strong> is a summit in Indiana. The Battle Point Trail covers 19.8 miles round trip (out-and-back) with about 318 feet of elevation gain \u2014 gentle grades, but the mileage is what makes it a Hard outing.</p>\n  <h3>The Route</h3><p>Most of the climbing comes early \u2014 the first half of the route does the bulk of the work before the grade eases. From the trailhead at about 745 feet, the route tops out near 1,010 feet. Along the way the route passes a viewpoint (Bonwell Hill Overlook) near mile 9.92 \u2014 useful checkpoints for judging your pace.</p>\n  <h3>Getting There</h3><p>The trailhead is at <a href=\"https://www.google.com/maps/dir/?api=1&destination=39.5059,-85.00065\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">39.5059, -85.00065</a> (tap for driving directions). Arrive early on weekends \u2014 trailhead lots at popular peaks fill quickly, and cell service is often unreliable once you leave the highway.</p>\n  <h3>When to Go</h3><p>Spring through fall is the main season. Conditions change fast in the shoulder months \u2014 check a point forecast for the summit, not the nearest town, before you commit.</p>\n  <h3>Know Before You Go</h3><p>The Hard rating comes from the National Park Service difficulty formula, which weighs total distance against elevation gain. Most hikers should budget about 7.0 hours of moving time; add margin for breaks, photos and the descent. Download the GPX track from this page before you go \u2014 cell coverage is unreliable in the mountains and a saved route works offline in any GPS app. Conditions change: verify current access, closures and weather with the official land manager before you go. Trail data is sourced from OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).</p>\n  <p>Looking to link objectives or plan a weekend? Nearby summits include The Mounds, Hog Back and Donalds Knoll \u2014 each has its own guide on this site.</p>\n</div>",
